<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battiad dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 631 – c. 440 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a> · Also known as Battiads</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battiad dynasty ruled the Greek city of Cyrene in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a> for about two centuries, from its foundation around 631 BCE by Battus I, a colonist from Thera. Its kings, named alternately Battus and Arcesilaus, extended the city's power, though their rule was limited by the reforms of Demonax in the 6th century BCE. The last king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcesilaus-iv">Arcesilaus IV</a>, was overthrown around 440 BCE.</p></div>
